         fhir:comment [ fhir:v "Element `NamingSystem.identifier` has a context of NamingSystem based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `NamingSystem`.\nElement `NamingSystem.identifier` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).\nTypically, this is used for identifiers that can go in an HL7 V3 II (instance identifier) data type, and can then identify this naming system outside of FHIR, where it is not possible to use the logical URI." ]
